      "content": "thanks. the contrast is definitely there. i want to make the local one even more specific though. to make it really punchy for the readers, can you rewrite the local resident's monologue so the language is even more \"street\"—using more dialect, maybe some slang typical of the urban areas that are usually gentrified? make it sound less \"standard english\" and more like someone who's really from the block and doesn't care about being polite to the newcomers. also, for the new resident, maybe make them sound a bit more obsessed with \"safety\" and how the area feels \"sketchy\" now compared to when they first saw the listing?",
